Rāma gently answers Sītā seeking to turn her back --- Rāma praises high-born Sītā and bids keep her own duty at home --- Rāma warns the forest holds many faults and brings only sorrow never ease --- Rāma warns mountain lions roar painfully in caves and falls --- Rāma warns weary sleep on broken leaf beds and fasting matted hair bark garments --- Rāma warns wind darkness hunger terrors snakes reptiles insects thorns tangle trees --- Rāma finds the forest wholly unfit for Sītā and refuses to lead her
